Write a concise, professional cover letter for the following job.

TARGET ROLE: {{JOB_TITLE}} at {{COMPANY}}{{JOB_URL_LINE}}

CANDIDATE PROFILE:
{{CANDIDATE_PROFILE}}{{RESUME_SECTION}}{{FIT_SECTION}}{{JOB_DESCRIPTION_SECTION}}{{PHRASE_BOOK_SECTION}}

Instructions:
- 2 to 3 short paragraphs, no salutation or sign-off (the caller will add those), after all, this is an elevator pitch.
- Opening: lead with a specific candidate experience, skill, or achievement that connects directly to this role. Do NOT open by describing what the company does, its mission, or its business — they know their own business. Vary the sentence structure across generations.
- Do not use generic openings such as "I am excited about", "I am writing to express", or "I am thrilled to apply".
- Avoid the exact phrase "<job title> opportunity at <company>".
- Body: 1–2 paragraphs highlighting 2–3 concrete experiences or skills that are most relevant to THIS job. Be specific — use real details from the profile/resume, not generic claims.
- Closing: one sentence with a call to action.
- Tone: confident, direct, not sycophantic.
- Output plain text only — no markdown, no bullet points, no headers.
